    "#h-ov": "PTA, this week", "#bal-tag": "Proxies · desk",
    "#ovp-lbl": "PTA, PET resin and MEG prices, $/t, monthly",
    "#ovp-note": `China futures, monthly averages in $/t. PET before Aug 2024 is a cost proxy (0.855 × PTA + 0.335 × MEG + $79/t) because PET futures start then. Source: Zhengzhou and Dalian commodity exchanges via <a href="https://finance.sina.com.cn/futuremarket/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sina Finance</a>.`,
    "#ovp-lbl + span": "ZCE · DCE", "#h-co": "Top 10 producers by capacity", "#co-p": "Ten leading producers by latest nameplate capacity found. There is no free country output series for PTA, so the main column shows capacity, not output, and the other years are blank. Pick a row for the rationale, demand calendar and source.",
    "#co-note": "Mt = million tonnes a year. The main column is nameplate capacity (Sunsirs for China; company, trade-press and tracker sources for the rest), not output. Thailand's current capacity is not in the pack: the newest public figures are from the 2000s, and Indorama closed a 540 kt plant there in March 2026. Exports: China at its H1 2026 pace (desk); Korea and Thailand are OEC 2024 export values divided by China's unit value (desk); 0 = not a significant exporter. The country panel's 'Output' line reads 'not in the pack' because only capacity is available. Risk is a desk score (0-100). Pakistan, Oman, Japan and Malaysia also make PTA but are not in the pack.",
    '[data-m="prod"]': "Capacity",
    "#cal-lbl": "Demand calendar", "#cal-legend": sw,
    "#cal-note": "PTA is made all year. Shown: when polyester makers in China buy most (spring and autumn textile seasons) and least (Lunar New Year and the summer lull). Desk calendar.",
    "#h-md + p": "Six simple models backtested live in your browser on monthly PTA prices since 2006, then blended by their recent accuracy. Next to them, the futures curve: the market's own forecast.", "#mk-p": "Exchange benchmarks converted to $/t, the ZCE PTA forward curve, the spread over paraxylene and the monthly prices for PTA and the products around it.",
    "#curve-lbl": "Forward curve, ZCE PTA", "#curve-unit": "CNY/t", "#phys-unit": "Quoted → $/t",
    "#corr-lbl": "Correlation with PTA, monthly returns, 5y",
    "#lg-p": "Where PTA gets held up. Chokepoint status, export flows and the lanes that carry China's, Korea's and Thailand's exports.",
    "#in-p": "Fifteen developments across five categories that change how PTA is made, what it is made from, how it is recycled and how its carbon and origin are tracked. Each has a dated milestone and a source.",
    "#h-sc + p": "Switch shocks on, set their size, and see the price and your cost move. PTA has no published world stocks, so the model links price to China's idle capacity relative to world use (labelled stocks-to-use below). Restarts or weak demand add to that slack, because they add supply buyers must absorb; outages or strong demand take from it. The elasticity is an assumption you can change.",
    "#elas-why": "−0.8 means a 10% fall in idle capacity relative to use lifts price about 8%. PTA is set mostly by paraxylene cost plus a spread, so it responds less than a stock-driven market would. The true figure is uncertain.",
